From ddf4748d31cb5dc65e7cd0b0c5b27b98d63ae880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 04:32:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] test(e2e): prefix-stability journeys for the messaging
 gateway, api_server and ACP

C17 covers the tui_gateway and the oneshot CLI only. The surfaces that
build a fresh agent per process had no restart journey, and that is
where #45499 and #104414 lived. Each new journey drives one durable
session through four process lives of one surface, with a parallel tool
batch and one compaction:

- messaging gateway: the real gateway.run.main behind the parity suite's
  recording Telegram adapter (it can now deliver several DMs per life),
  /compress sent as a DM;
- api_server: POST /v1/runs addressed by the client's session_id; the
  provider reports context pressure, so the next turn auto-compacts;
- ACP: session/new, then session/load in a fresh `hermes acp`, /compress
  as ACP's own slash command.

The messaging gateway and api_server journeys pass. The ACP journey fails
and is gated with known_gate on its own signature. After /compress, the
first request of a reloaded session misses the whole prefix, for two
reasons. The compacted transcript is not persisted (#76215; fixes in
review: #76224, #88364). And the prompt rebuilt at the compaction nests the
cached one, because acp_adapter/commands.py passes
system_message=agent._cached_system_prompt to compress_now (the #15281
shape). A new assertion pins the second cause on every surface: the
prompt rebuilt at a compaction never contains the previous one.

The ACP journey spawns and initializes `hermes acp` through the parity
driver's new spawn_acp/close_acp, which drive_acp now uses too.

Harness changes: model_payload skips the gateway's session_meta row,
which is never sent and which every production reader filters. Usage and
integrity are now asserted before the gated prefix block, so a gate
cannot mask them.

Refs #76215

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
